    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d591">

                <pb facs="0665" n="653" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg653"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.01/3477: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-02-29T00:00:00+01:00">February 29,
                            1944—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received February 29—10:14 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1662. For the Acting Secretary. In answer to your 1448 of February 26, I do not
                    believe that the Prime Minister has to date concluded that the French Committee
                    should be accorded recognition <pb facs="0666" n="654" xml:id="pg654"/> as a
                    provisional government. He has been more friendly toward the Committee since his
                    return from North Africa. I found that Eden’s statement on February 23 in
                        Parliament<anchor n="28" xml:id="d591-f1"/> was largely written by the Prime
                    Minister.</p>
                <p>I am certain that the British would not want to act without our collaboration and
                    support.</p>
                <p>I am sending you Eden’s statement about France in my immediately following cable
                    No. 1663.<anchor n="29" xml:id="d591-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d591-f1" n="28" xml:id="d591-f1-content">
                <p>See <hi rendition="#italic">Parliamentary Delates</hi>, House of Commons, 5th
                    series, vol. 397, cols. 929–933.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d591-f2" n="29" xml:id="d591-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
